    "body": "By forcing I was thinking about \"this extended attribute is valid only on ...\" type of thing rather than forcing syntactically. That should be doable.\r\n\r\n> This means that in an argument `[AttrForArg, AttrForType] Type? x`, `[AttrForArg, AttrForType]` _cannot_ bind tighter than `?`, because `AttrForArg` needs to apply to the whole argument.\r\n\r\nIt can be `[AttrForArg] ([AttrForType] Type)? x` right? Yes it's kinda awkward to read, but maybe less ambiguous?",
