    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T17:43:36Z",
    "body": "About this from your Claude session:\r\n```\r\n  - index.bs:6539, index.bs:6557 — The new wording \"the type of an argument |A|\" / \"the type of a [=dictionary member=] |M|\" now also covers optional arguments and required members, so [Clamp] optional long x and [Clamp] required long m; become valid.\r\n    - This reverses #691, which was closed because the old wording already limited this to non-optional arguments and non-required members. bzbarsky said [Clamp] optional short is not correct, and domenic agreed.\r\n    - It also contradicts step 2's own example (optional [XAttr] long arg, required [XAttr] long member).\r\n    - Fix: \"…an argument |A| that is not declared with the <emu-t>optional</emu-t> keyword…\" and \"…a [=dictionary member=] |M| that is not [=dictionary member/required=]…\". Don't write \"not an [=optional argument=]\": a final variadic argument counts as\r\n      optional, so [Clamp] long... values would lose its [Clamp].\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote that there are some specs that do put the extended attribute before `optional`/`required`:\r\n- https://serial.spec.whatwg.org/#serialoptions-dictionary\r\n- https://www.w3.org/TR/webcodecs/#video-encoder-config\r\n\r\nRestricting that would need also updates to those specs and _maybe_ to implementations? Happy to do it and open issues for those specs, just double-checking that you actually want it.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
